                                                    "text": "param mode_blend 0.5 @min 0 @max 1",
                                                    "varname": "mode_blend"
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "id": "obj-25",
                                                    "linecount": 53,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 733.0 ],
                                                    "text": "================================================================================\n05_phaseshaper_supersaw_tri — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nImplements the two flagship Roland JP-8000 phaseshaping algorithms plus the Variable-Slope Tilted Triangle phaseshaper from Kleimola, Lazzarini, Timoney, and Välimäki (SMC 2010, Sections 2.4, 3.5, and 3.6):\n1. Triangle Modulation (Eq. 26): Folds a doubled triangular phase via a ceiling staircase function to generate an odd-harmonic-only spectrum where the 3rd partial dominates and upper formants sweep dramatically.\n2. Single-Oscillator Ripple Supersaw (Eq. 28 & Fig. 13): Uses nested real-valued modulo operations (gripple) inside a single sinusoidal waveshaper to synthesize a thick, 7-saw detuned unison pad phase-locked to the live tuba note.\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Audio Input (ideally fed from 01_harmonic_isolator; in2 silent for 250 ms -> in1 is used for both sides)\n- in3: Tracked Pitch in Hz. Drives a phase-locked loop: a strictly monotonic phasor at f0, locked to the phase of the tuba's bandpassed fundamental (about 8 Hz loop). Outside 20..1000 Hz an internal zero-crossing tracker is used. (Earlier versions took the raw analytic phase of the whole signal, which wrapped about twice per period on low notes and ran backwards on up to 10% of samples.)\n- in4: Optional 1-Bar Phasor [0..1] (if moving, locks the Supersaw m1 quadrature detune animation to the bar; when in4 has not moved for 100 ms an internal 0.35 Hz LFO takes over)\n- out1 / out2: Stereo Phaseshaped Output (wet only; follows the tuba's envelope with a 15 ms follower)\n- Level: on the sousa_mic.aif take (-32 dB RMS in), about -35 dB RMS with mode_blend 0 and -32 dB RMS with mode_blend 1 (offline render of the real RNBO code). The Triangle Modulation output is now centred: as written, Eq. 26 spanned (-3, -1] and pushed out1 to +1.4 dBFS of mostly DC.\n\nPARAMETERS (4)\n\n1. shape_mod\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0\n   - Taper: Linear mapping to the paper's exact active parameter ranges: a_TM in [0.70, 1.00] for Triangle Modulation (Eq. 26) and phase extension a1 in [1.15, 2.25] for Supersaw (Eq. 28).\n   - Function: Drives the V-fold depth of the Triangle Modulator and the harmonic brightness/sync discontinuity of the Ripple Supersaw.\n\n2. ripple_detune\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (maps to ripple modulus m1 in [0.18, 0.80] with quadrature L/R animation)\n   - Taper: Linear depth scaling of the ripple modulus m1 (Paper Fig. 12: m1 = 0.25 to 0.75, m2 = 0.88).\n   - Function: Controls the density and stereo unison beating of the ripple-edged phaseshaper.\n\n3. tilt_duty\n   - Range: 0.10 to 0.90 (Duty Width w of Parabolic Tilted Triangle Phase svtri, Eq. 16)\n   - Taper: Linear around 0.50 (at 0.50 the phase ramp is symmetric; moving toward 0.10 or 0.90 tilts the up/down ramp slopes, shifting formants and eliminating every 4th harmonic outside the formant band).\n   - Function: Pre-warps the extracted tuba phasor through the paper's parabolic variable-slope triangle generator before entering the Triangle Mod or Supersaw stage.\n\n4. mode_blend\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0.0 = 100% JP-8000 Triangle Modulation, 1.0 = 100% Ripple Supersaw)\n   - Taper: Linear crossfade.\n   - Function: Seamlessly morphs between hollow, 3rd-harmonic-heavy Triangle Modulation growls and massive stereo Supersaw brass chords.\n",
                                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                                }
                                            }
